Triton attention: opt-in, INFO-once 2D/3D dispatch screening.

A runtime-only diagnostic that shows which path a real multi-query shape took,
without changing either Triton kernel or its launch configuration. Off by
default; when on it logs once per distinct shape and worker process from the
Python dispatch boundary, before launch. It reads CPU metadata only, so it is
safe during CUDA-graph capture. Turn it off for performance measurements.

The flag is registered so vLLM accepts it, but excluded from compile_factors
because it does not shape generated code: a traced and an untraced run of the
same configuration share one compile cache.

